# KNOWN GAP `todo/t1313` — RUST LANE. A `Box[T]` passed to a `^` (move)
# PARAMETER double-frees. Six lines, a primitive payload, no nesting, no
# deref, no `.clone()`.
#
#   C:    build rc 0, run rc 134, `free(): invalid pointer`
#   LLVM: build rc 0, run rc 134, `double free or corruption (out)`
#
# ⚠ THIS IS WIDER THAN THE FILED `todo/t0010`, WHICH IS WHY IT IS ITS OWN
# ITEM RATHER THAN A SECOND CELL ON THAT ONE. `t0010`'s repro needs
# `(*b).clone()` on an owned-and-dead `Box[Leaf]` — a deref, a clone and a
# struct payload. Strip all three and the double free is still there. The
# discriminator `t0010` names (move-eligibility of the Box AT THE CLONE) cannot
# be the discriminator here, because there is no clone.
#
# ⭐ WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND ITS SIZE: a `Box` exists precisely to make
# double-free impossible by construction — single owner, no implicit-copy path,
# `^` or `.clone()` required at every consuming position. This is that
# guarantee failing in the lowering of the very operator that enforces it, on
# the most ordinary possible shape.
#
# ⚠ MEASURED ON BOTH SIDES OF `todo/t1077`'s fix and IDENTICAL (rc 134 before,
# rc 134 after, both backends), so it is a pre-existing sibling and not inflow
# from that change. It is also why `t1077`'s fixture set has no `^`-parameter
# cell: writing one would pin a defect that fix cannot move.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: 1
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.

int take(Box[int] ^b):
    return 1

void main():
    Box[int] b = Box[int](7)
    print(take(^b))
